{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "slug": "factions/humans",
      "type": "faction",
      "tension": 0.4,
      "facts": {
        "role": "recent arrivals",
        "status": "extant",
        "note": "Colony charter 'Drosselmeyer', arrived 11 years ago chasing the same marrow the dead built on."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "civs/the-velt",
      "type": "faction",
      "tension": 0.8,
      "facts": {
        "alien_type": "crystalline-slow-life",
        "status": "fallen",
        "metabolism": "lithic, one thought per century",
        "note": "Grew cities by accreting silicate over deep time; mined the world's marrow to quicken their own slow minds."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "civs/the-choir",
      "type": "faction",
      "tension": 0.85,
      "facts": {
        "alien_type": "psychic-gestalt",
        "status": "fallen",
        "form": "no bodies, only a shared standing-wave of minds",
        "note": "A hive of voices that lived in the planet's resonance; heard the wound before anyone dug it."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "figures/archivist-soln",
      "type": "colonist",
      "facts": {
        "role": "human xeno-archivist",
        "note": "Catalogs Velt glass; first to notice the cities are screaming at a frequency she can't hear."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "figures/the-last-cantor",
      "type": "colonist",
      "facts": {
        "role": "final coherent voice of the Choir",
        "species": "choir-remnant",
        "note": "A single surviving node of the gestalt, looping its last warning."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "figures/velt-deepwright-kael",
      "type": "colonist",
      "facts": {
        "role": "Velt mine-architect (petrified)",
        "note": "Designed the marrow-bores; his crystallized body is the deepest artifact."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "locations/the-marrow-vein",
      "type": "location",
      "tension": 0.85,
      "facts": {
        "note": "The deep extraction shaft; the wound. Still warm, still humming."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "locations/glasshalls-of-velt",
      "type": "location",
      "tension": 0.7,
      "facts": {
        "note": "Velt city flash-frozen mid-thought into clear glass."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "locations/the-silent-choir-amphitheater",
      "type": "location",
      "tension": 0.75,
      "facts": {
        "note": "Resonant cavern where the Choir sang itself to death trying to drown the wound."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "locations/colony-drosselmeyer",
      "type": "location",
      "tension": 0.45,
      "facts": {
        "note": "Human landing site, built on a marrow seam they don't yet understand."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "powers/resonant-sympathy",
      "type": "power",
      "tension": 0.6,
      "facts": {
        "kind": "psychic",
        "note": "Hearing/steering the planetary standing-wave; the Choir's native sense, leaking now into sensitive humans."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "powers/lithomancy",
      "type": "power",
      "tension": 0.55,
      "facts": {
        "kind": "psychic",
        "note": "Velt deep-time cognition — reading intent stored in stone over centuries."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-marrow-was-alive",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.65,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "role": "cause",
        "text": "The 'ore' the Velt mined was not mineral. It was the dormant nerve-marrow of a single planet-spanning organism, asleep since before the suns cooled."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/extraction-was-amputation",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.75,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "role": "escalation",
        "text": "Every bore-shaft severed living tissue. The world did not die — it woke, in pieces, in pain, and began to dream of the things cutting into it."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-wound-sang",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.8,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "role": "escalation",
        "text": "The severed marrow discharged its agony as a psychic standing-wave. The Choir heard it first — and could not stop hearing it."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-choir-tried-to-sing-it-down",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.85,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "role": "point-of-no-return",
        "text": "The Choir threw its entire gestalt against the wound, singing a counter-wave to lull the planet back to sleep. Instead the planet learned the Choir's frequency — and answered in their own voices."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-resonance-cascade",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.88,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "role": "collapse",
        "text": "The amplified wave reached the marrow seams running under every Velt city. The crystalline minds, tuned to stone, vitrified in a single shared instant — and the Choir dissolved into the song they could no longer leave."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "artifacts/kaels-bore-codex",
      "type": "artifact",
      "tension": 0.7,
      "facts": {
        "archetype": "lost-codex",
        "tier": "relic",
        "note": "Velt deepwright's etched-glass mining ledger; reads like blueprints, ends like a confession."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "artifacts/the-still-tuning-fork",
      "type": "artifact",
      "tension": 0.8,
      "facts": {
        "archetype": "living-relic",
        "tier": "relic",
        "note": "A Choir resonance-anchor; still faintly vibrating with the counter-wave they died singing."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "artifacts/the-marrow-shard",
      "type": "artifact",
      "tension": 0.9,
      "facts": {
        "archetype": "cursed-idol",
        "tier": "relic",
        "note": "A fist-sized splinter of severed marrow. Warm. Beats. Wants to be put back."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "artifacts/cantors-final-loop",
      "type": "artifact",
      "tension": 0.82,
      "facts": {
        "archetype": "prophecy-object",
        "tier": "relic",
        "note": "A standing-wave knot holding the Last Cantor's final 7 seconds, replaying forever."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "artifacts/the-vitrified-map",
      "type": "artifact",
      "tension": 0.7,
      "facts": {
        "archetype": "key-map",
        "tier": "relic",
        "note": "A Velt city frozen so cleanly it became a literal 3D map of every marrow seam on the world."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "artifacts/the-silence-engine",
      "type": "artifact",
      "tension": 0.85,
      "facts": {
        "archetype": "weapon-relic",
        "tier": "relic",
        "note": "A Velt-built dampener meant to mute the wound; it works once, then sings back twice as loud."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/velt-thought-in-stone",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.5,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The Velt did not write; they thought INTO silicate over centuries. To read their glass is to overhear a hundred-year sentence."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/marrow-quickened-the-velt",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.6,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "Refined marrow let a Velt think in days instead of decades. Their golden age was an addiction."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-choir-had-no-bodies",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.55,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The Choir was never matter — only a self-sustaining pattern of minds. Anything that could overwrite the pattern could erase them entirely."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-counter-wave-failed",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.78,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The fork's vibration is the Choir's lullaby, preserved. Played near the wound, it does not soothe — the planet sings it back, perfected, predatory."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-marrow-remembers-the-cut",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.85,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The shard is not dead tissue. It is awake, and it remembers being severed. Held long enough, it teaches the holder resonant-sympathy whether they want it or not."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-shard-wants-reunion",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.8,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "Every marrow fragment strains toward the vein. Reunite enough and the organism wakes whole — the colony sits on the largest seam left."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-last-warning",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.83,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The Cantor's final loop is not grief. Decoded, it is an instruction: DO NOT DIG. DO NOT SING. LET IT SLEEP."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/every-city-sat-on-a-seam",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.7,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The vitrified map proves the Velt built atop the marrow on purpose — proximity sped their thoughts. They paved their graves."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-seams-run-under-the-colony",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.75,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The largest unbroken seam on the map runs directly beneath Colony Drosselmeyer's foundations."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/silence-is-borrowed",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.8,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The Silence Engine buys quiet by storing the wound's song. Its capacity is finite; what it holds, it eventually returns, louder."
      }
    },
    {
      "slug": "lore/the-velt-built-the-engine-too-late",
      "type": "lore",
      "tension": 0.72,
      "facts": {
        "subtype": "fragment",
        "revealed": false,
        "text": "The dampener was a deathbed project. By the time it worked, the cascade was already under the cities."
      }
    }
  ],
